# SESSION_NOTES-S269-through-S258.md.verify.sh — the losslessness proof for this shard.
#
# Generated by Session 277 (the ELEVENTH trim). Re-runnable, read-only, exits non-zero on failure.
#
#   bash <this>              prove the eleventh trim was lossless AND landed where it was declared
#   bash <this> --self-test  prove this proof can FAIL (109 mutants; exit 2 if any survives)
#
# Descended from Session 266's SESSION_NOTES-S257-through-S249.md.verify.sh, itself descended from
# Session 256's, 245's, 242's, 239's, 235's, 231's, 228's, 224's and 222's — read those for the
# rationale behind L0-L3, L4, L5-L7, L8-L9, L10-L11, L12, L13 and L14, and the ninth's for the byte
# rule and for every operand it re-targeted off the retired pointer block. Shards are WRITE-ONCE:
# this proof pins ITS OWN cut key and does not re-prove the earlier shards' cuts. Run all eleven
# shard proofs, and both collapse proofs, which own the front-matter table this cut adds a row to.
#
# NO ASSERTION IS ADDED HERE, AND NO INHERITED ONE IS REWRITTEN. The operator's ruling F
# (docs/planning/ledger-budgets-review.md §13.1, 2026-09-07) ended the assertion-per-trim
# convention, and the ninth proof's L11 already enforces the byte rule this cut obeys. L0-L14
# below are the tenth proof's, function for function: the AST of every function but self_test is
# identical (measured; one docstring, compose_row's, which named the ninth proof, was re-dated).
# What changes is DECLARATION, and the list was MEASURED the way CLAUDE.md prescribes, not
# recalled: the tenth proof's declared literals run against the working tree at HEAD (01a39dd),
# each one present at its trim commit (49d23b7) and absent now flagged: 0 of 111 (36 required and
# 20 forbidden REACH strings, 3 SIZE_PROSE and 3 SPAN_PROSE literals outside the banner, 40
# LINEAGE_PROSE literals, the old and new text of each of 4 substitutions, and the row); the four
# substitution anchors the tenth trim itself consumed are absent by construction. A second run
# against this cut's tree flags every literal that stopped matching because of it: 26 of 111:
# 22 are the tenth cut's own counts, spans, sizes and ordinals (19 required REACH strings, 2
# SIZE_PROSE, 1 LINEAGE), and 4 are front matter (three substitutions' replacement texts, and
# row 10's `this commit`).
#
# WHAT CHANGED, AND WHY EACH CHANGE IS A RE-DECLARATION RATHER THAN A WEAKENING.
#
#   CUT KEY, ROUTING   twelve records archived (269 -> 258), none of them a claim stub; one shard
#                      clause added, the live clause moved to 270. The retained side holds one
#                      stub (277, this session's, still a stub at the trim commit) and seven
#                      non-stub records. L11's floor reads the retained side alone.
#   REACH              re-declared for eleven shards. The four files are the same four: the seventh
#                      re-derivation of the sweep found no fifth, and the sweep itself is published
#                      in Session 277's close-out record rather than restated here.
#   ANCESTOR_PROOFS    gains the tenth proof, frozen at 49d23b7 — its only commit, measured
#                      rather than assumed: `git log -- <that proof>` prints one commit, and its
#                      blob equals the file on disk.
#   SIZES, SIZE_PROSE, ROW, SPAN_PROSE, BANNER   this cut's own figures, each derived. SPAN_CENSUS
#                      (and M85/M93's fixture sentence) are the tenth proof's, unchanged.
#   L14's DECLARATION  gains the tenth shard — the handover L14/set exists to force: four literals,
#                      the BACKLOG chain widened from eight totals to nine, and the census
#                      sentence with them.
#   FRONT_SUBST        four substitutions, none of them reusable from the tenth proof: each of its
#                      four anchors was consumed by the tenth trim, so each of these is anchored on
#                      text the tenth trim WROTE. Three are the tenth's kinds again (the write-once
#                      ordinal, the trim count, and row 10's `this commit` resolved to the hash the
#                      legend promises the next trim will supply). The second is smaller than the
#                      tenth's: that trim discharged the bequest block, so there is nothing to
#                      discharge now and only the addressee moves, to the twelfth trim. Nothing
#                      derives the hash — the census guard skips its cell by design — so it is
#                      declared by hand and was measured: `git log --diff-filter=A` on the tenth
#                      shard prints 49d23b7 and nothing else.
#   THE MUTANTS        109 stay 109. Every fixture that quoted the tenth cut's own spans, sizes and
#                      ordinals was re-pointed to this cut's, and the figure-bearing ones (M42,
#                      M64-M66, M82, M95, M96, M102) now DERIVE their text from SIZES, SIZE_PROSE and
#                      LINEAGE_PROSE instead of typing it. M58 has ZERO slack at this cut: it keeps
#                      EIGHT records, SEVEN of them non-stub, so its derived floor is 8 and the
#                      assertion that the count still meets it reads 8 <= 8; a typed 7 is met by both
#                      the count and the classifier and the mutant would survive, exactly as it would
#                      have at the tenth, whose slack was also zero (any cut that retains exactly one
#                      claim stub has none). M67 and M107
#                      move the banner's heading count as a WORD, and this cut's count, twelve, is the
#                      last entry of WORDS: M67 types "eleven record", M107 "twelvefold record" (a word
#                      that CONTAINS the right one, as "nineteen" did). M109 and M68 are unchanged in
#                      code: both index the declared substitution that resolves the previous row's
#                      hash, which is now row 10's. Per mutant, the arms that catch it are identical
#                      to the tenth proof's once a shard filename inside a code is normalised —
#                      measured by diffing the two `--self-test` listings: three lines differ (M16,
#                      M24, M55), each only in a filename, and fourteen labels differ (M24 and M55
#                      among them, so the two counts overlap), each naming this cut's spans or
#                      ordinals.
#
# MEASURED COVERAGE — produced by running both loops against FROZEN artifacts, the exit code checked on
# every run: 0 or 2, never anything else, which would be a broken run scored as a clean one
# (learning #190). The harness is described in Session 277's close-out record; run on the TENTH proof it
# reproduced that proof's published whole-assertion lists below exactly, which is its validity check.
#
#   WHOLE ASSERTION — neuter `fails += Ln(...)` to `pass`; what survives is what Ln ALONE catches:
#
#     L0 (none)   L1 (none)*   L2 M10-M15,M40,M51,M68,M98-M100,M105,M109   L3 (none)   L4 (none)
#     L5 M18-M23,M25,M26,M38,M39,M47,M52   L6 M27   L7 M29,M30   L8 M31-M34,M41,M43-M46,M50
#     L9 M35-M37   L10 M53-M55   L11 M56-M59,M84   L12 M60-M67,M73,M81,M82,M96,M97,M101,M102,M107
#     L13 M69-M72,M74-M80,M83,M85,M103,M108   L14 M86-M95,M104,M106
#
#     * L1's blank entry is NOT a licence to remove it. L3 and L4 catch everything L1 catches, but
#       L1 is what the fifth trim's narrowing of L2/b3 rests on. Read '(none)' as 'overlapped'.
#
#   PER ARM — 68 failure-emitting statements in L0-L14 (`out.append(...)` to `pass`, a non-empty
#   `return [...]` to `return []`, type-preserving — learning #191). 48 of them uniquely catch a
#   mutant. A first sweep found L2/b0, L2_ROW_MISSING and L2/b1 reachable only in company, and M98,
#   M99 and M100 were built to isolate them. The 20 still without a sole catcher are the tenth
#   proof's 20, arm for arm (both proofs run through the same loop on the same day: 83 variants
#   each, no run broken, every exit code 0 or 2), so its three causes carry over verbatim:
#
#   * OVERLAPPED BY INHERITANCE (7) — L0's trailing-block arm, L1, L3's three and L4's two. Each
#     fires on the mutants aimed at it; the derivation arms (L12/row, L13) fire alongside. A cut
#     shifted with EVERY declaration moved to match would be L4's alone; building it re-declares
#     the whole proof, and is recorded rather than built.
#   * PROVABLY SUBSUMED (10) — L2/b2 (a vanished line always changes the residue b1 compares, and
#     with the row missing b1 yields to L2_ROW_MISSING); L5/2's frontier arm and both L5/3 arms (the
#     table copy derives its frontier as newest archived + 1, and this shard's clause cannot move
#     without its row, which L12/row composes from the records); the four UNREADABLE arms of L8,
#     L12, L13 and L14 (no file is read by one assertion alone); L9's and L14/blob's no-add-commit
#     arms (a shard with no add-commit is unmeasurable to both).
#   * VACUITY GUARDS (3), never meant to fire alone — L0's no-records arm, L5/4's no-numeric-ids arm
#     and L13's empty-records-zone arm.
#
# The grammar is FROZEN into this file on purpose: a later change to the trim design must not
# silently change what THIS shard's proof means.
